---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CLI reference"
  description="Reference for the llmdoc dual-repository CLI: binding, retrieval, diagnostics, semantic commit, candidate capture, convergence, migration, and host integration."
  section="cli"
>
  <h1>CLI reference</h1>
  <p>Invoke the external CLI as <code>npx -y @vegetablebird6/llmdoc &lt;command&gt;</code>. Pin the version in the package spec when a workflow must be reproducible. Retrieval commands accept <code>--json</code>, <code>--budget</code>, and <code>--limit</code>; <code>--cursor</code> continues truncated output.</p>

  <h2>Bind and initialize</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>bind --source &lt;dir&gt; --knowledge &lt;dir&gt; [--nested]</code></dt><dd>Associate a source repository with an existing independent knowledge repository. The association is recorded in the user-level registry, and llmdoc never writes to the source repository.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>init --source &lt;dir&gt; --knowledge &lt;dir&gt; [--nested]</code></dt><dd>Create the knowledge Git repository, the layout, the initial knowledge commit, and the user binding. Existing non-empty targets are never overwritten.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Discover and read</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>tree</code></dt><dd>Knowledge map by topic, with root documents.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>index [--topic …] [--kind …]</code></dt><dd>Document metadata without reading bodies.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>show &lt;path…&gt;</code></dt><dd>Read selected document bodies.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>search &lt;query&gt;</code></dt><dd>Lexical search with Chinese word segmentation and an explicitly reported CJK-bigram fallback after zero lexical recall.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>context --files &lt;src…&gt;</code></dt><dd>Map each source file to the documents to read, including the <code>requires</code> closure, while reporting unmapped inputs explicitly.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Diagnose state</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>validate</code></dt><dd>Deterministic front matter, link, relation, source-scope, and schema checks against the fixed source snapshot. It never advances a revision.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>status</code></dt><dd>Source blockers, knowledge state, and review obligations. Source blockers are reported separately from document status.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>delta [--scope &lt;id…&gt;]</code></dt><dd>Documents that need semantic review after source or knowledge changes.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Commit semantically</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>review [--confirm &lt;reviewId&gt;] [--set &lt;id&gt;=&lt;conclusion&gt;…] [--global]</code></dt><dd>Generate a temporary Review Manifest for the fixed source and knowledge revisions, or confirm its semantic conclusions. Conclusions are <code>changed</code>, <code>unchanged</code>, or <code>insufficient</code>.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>commit --review &lt;reviewId&gt;</code></dt><dd>Seal a confirmed Review Manifest into a single knowledge commit. There is no bare verified flag.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Candidates and maintenance</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>capture [--title] [--note] [--from] [--body] [--source-revision]</code></dt><dd>Persist an unverified candidate under <code>inbox/</code> without touching formal knowledge or the source repository.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>update [--promote …] [--reject …] [--prepare] [--global]</code></dt><dd>Review inbox candidates and apply promote/reject decisions, forming an unconfirmed Review Manifest. It never marks anything current.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>prune [--report] [--remove &lt;id…&gt;] [--global]</code></dt><dd>Report conservative convergence candidates, or remove eligible documents and repair every inbound relation and link.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>migrate --knowledge &lt;dir&gt; [--source] [--legacy] [--dry-run] [--nested]</code></dt><dd>Explicitly migrate a legacy V3 layout into a new independent knowledge repository. This is the only command that reads <code>.mdx</code>, <code>CodeRef</code>, <code>code.paths</code>, <code>llmdoc/meta.json</code>, or <code>llmdoc.config.json</code>.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Host integration</h2>
  <dl class="commands">
    <div><dt><code>hook session-start | stop | compact</code></dt><dd>Read-only, fail-open diagnostics. It reports review obligations and source blockers, never writes source or knowledge, and never initializes a binding.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><code>serve [--port &lt;port&gt;]</code></dt><dd>Start the read-only viewer of the fixed Knowledge HEAD on <code>127.0.0.1</code>, with the same tri-state and double revision as the CLI.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Write flow</h2>
  <pre><code>capture → update --promote/--reject → review → review --confirm &lt;reviewId&gt; → commit --review &lt;reviewId&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>A formal update, review, or seal requires a valid source HEAD and a fully clean source worktree/index. The knowledge worktree may be dirty; the knowledge index may not have anything staged. Any edit after confirmation invalidates the manifest.</p>

  <p>All fixed CLI interface text is English. Chinese queries and repository document content remain supported and are returned unchanged.</p>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .commands { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .commands div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(210px, 0.8fr) 1fr; gap: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0.9rem 0; }
  .commands dt, .commands dd { margin: 0; }
  .commands dd { color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .commands div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; } }
</style>
